              "title": "BITSAT 2024 (Memory Based Paper 3)"
            }
          ],
          "question": {
            "text": "$A B C$ is a triangular park with $A B=A C=100 \\mathrm{~m}$. A TV tower stands at the mid-point of $B C$. The angles of elevation of the top of the tower at $A$, $B, C$ are $45^{\\circ}, 60^{\\circ}, 60^{\\circ}$ respectively. The height of the tower is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "ZObfB",
              "text": "50 m",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "mJVAF",
              "text": "$50 \\sqrt{3} \\mathrm{~m}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": true
            },
            {
              "id": "JXf6I",
              "text": "$50 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{~m}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            },
            {
              "id": "8bnN6",
              "text": "$50(3-\\sqrt{3}) \\mathrm{m}$",
              "image": null,
              "isCorrect": false
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "According to question,\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/5y1wsg7K9bwn0ZuQXOhXNn-7N9PFZP4Ui3BT9LeBulw.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nLet $D E=h$ and $C D=D B=x$\nIn $\\triangle E B D, \\quad \\tan 60^{\\circ}=\\frac{h}{x} \\Rightarrow x=\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}$\nNow, in $\\triangle A D E$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\tan 45^{\\circ}=\\frac{E D}{D A} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad D A=h\n\\end{aligned}$\nIn $\\triangle A B D$, by applying Pythagoras theorem\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad\\left(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\right)^2+h^2=100^2 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{4 h^2}{3}=10000 \\quad \\Rightarrow h=50 \\sqrt{3}\n\\end{aligned}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
