          },
          "evalStatus": "notAttempted",
          "lastPracticed": null
        },
        {
          "_id": "64c0e8346f5bfc7ab78aeb85",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "64c0e679aef333185c6bb44d",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2022-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2022",
              "title": "BITSAT 2022"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 3,
          "question": {
            "text": "Let $\\alpha$ be the solution of $16^{\\sin ^2 \\theta}+16^{\\cos ^2 \\theta}=10$ in $\\left(0, \\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$. If the shadow of a vertical pole is $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$ of its height, then the altitude of the sun is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "CD83W",
              "text": "\r\n$\\alpha$\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "5PAPU",
              "text": "\r\n$\\frac{\\alpha}{2}$\r\n",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "Pkc7b",
              "text": "\r\n$2 \\alpha$\r\n",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "cbONo",
              "text": "\r\n$\\frac{\\alpha}{3}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "We have,\r\n$16^{\\sin ^2 \\theta}+16^{\\cos ^2 \\theta}=10$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 16^{\\sin ^2 \\theta}+16^{1-\\sin ^2 \\theta}=10$\r\n$\\Rightarrow x+\\frac{16}{x}=10$, where $x=16^{\\sin ^2 \\theta}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad x^2-10 x+16=0 \\Rightarrow x=2,8$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad 16^{\\sin ^2 \\theta}=2,8 \\Rightarrow 2^{4 \\sin ^2 \\theta}=2,2^3$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 4 \\sin ^2 \\theta=1,3 \\Rightarrow \\sin ^2 \\theta=\\frac{1}{4},\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)^2$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\sin \\theta=\\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\Rightarrow \\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{6}, \\frac{\\pi}{3}$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/S5pOq2wkF-enUh0phx2RJpTLusnmaGSnw_vsT1ydx70.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\nLet the altitude of the sun be $\\theta$. Then,\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n& & \\tan \\theta & =\\frac{h}{h / \\sqrt{3}} \\Rightarrow \\tan \\theta=\\sqrt{3} \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow \\quad & & \\theta & =\\pi / 3 \\Rightarrow \\theta=2 \\alpha\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n$$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
          "questionStructure": [
            "default"
          ],
